    "open_questions": [
      "Itchycoo Park (1967): the only drum tab (Songsterr 2218570) is a 'regenerated' track, one bar looped with no hat, and the record's phased drums could not confirm it. Not written as a song.",
      "All or Nothing: the tab stops at bar 51 of about 87; the second verse and the last choruses are laid out from the lyric with the tab's bars.",
      "Stay With Me: the tabs write eighths on the hat, Jones sixteenths 'all the way through'; the style follows him. Check against isolated stems if any appear.",
      "Read his memoir, Let the Good Times Roll (2018), and the Hellier interviews for his own account of Tin Soldier, Itchycoo Park's phasing and the Who years.",
      "Which kit on which record: the silver glitter and black Ludwigs and the Rogers of the Small Faces, the Premiers, Yamahas and blonde Ludwigs of the Faces; dates per record not found.",
      "Who cites him besides Phil Rudd and Zak Starkey: not searched further."
    ]
  },
