    "roles": ["band_member", "session", "touring"],
    "summary": "A founder of the Small Faces in East London in 1965, at sixteen; the mod band's drummer on All or Nothing, Itchycoo Park, Tin Soldier and Ogdens' Nut Gone Flake; then the Faces with Rod Stewart and Ronnie Wood (1969-1975), and the Who's drummer after Keith Moon (1978-1988), on Face Dances and It's Hard. Raised on jazz and Booker T. & the MG's ('Al Jackson will remain my hero'); hit hard, played laid back, and moved the backbeat between the snare and the floor tom. Plain grooves with the kick pushing the 'and's and rolls of sixteenths into the next line; straighter and less frenetic than Moon, which Daltrey never forgave. Later the Law and the Jones Gang; in the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame with the Small Faces/Faces (2012)."
  },
